    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §207-a, Gen Muni L (as proposed in S.6144-A & A.7646-A)",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1308\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to ensuring paid\nfirefighters of a county airport or county aviation department which\nperform fire response or fire rescue duties are eligible for equal bene-\nfits as other paid firefighters\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2020,\nc.325.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by clarifying that the\nlegislation applies specifically to paid firefighters, which was the\nintent of the original legislation.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 34 of 2020, the Executive and the Legislature\nreached an agreement to clarify that the underlying legislation applies\nonly to paid firefighters.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 325 of the Laws of 2020.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nAn act to amend the General Municipal Law, in relation to ensuring paid\nfirefighters of a county airport or county aviation department which\nperform fire response or fire rescue duties are eligible for equal bene-\nfits as other paid firefighters.\n",
